<title>USA: Taro gets marketing OK for vaginal cream.</title>
<headline>Taro gets marketing OK for vaginal cream.</headline>
<dateline>HAWTHORNE, N.Y. 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taro Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd said Tuesday that its antifungal vaginal cream has received abbreviated new drug application approval from the Food and Drug Administration.</p>
<p>The product, Miconazole Nitrate Vaginal Cream USP 2 percent, is used to treat vaginal yeast infections.</p>
<p>Taro said the market in the United States for treatment of vaginal yeast infections has been estimated by industry sources to be about $240 million.</p>
</text>
